{"nodes": [{"id": "questions_21_deployment_question", "label": "Q21: How to deploy microservices", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "questions_21_deployment_independent_deployment", "label": "Independent deployment per service", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One pipeline per service triggered by that service's path, so a change to Risk does not rebuild the other eight. If two services must ship together they are one service."}, {"id": "questions_21_deployment_one_image_all_environments", "label": "One image, all environments", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Config from environment variables and secrets, never baked into the image; a separate image per environment means testing something you will not ship, and appsettings.Production.json in the image makes a config change need a rebuild."}, {"id": "questions_21_deployment_backwards_compatibility", "label": "Backwards compatibility for one release", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nine services cannot deploy atomically, so version N and N+1 run simultaneously: add a column before writing to it, add an event field before requiring it, never rename and replace in one release. Contract snapshot tests make that a conscious decision rather than an accident."}, {"id": "questions_21_deployment_expand_contract", "label": "Expand/contract migrations", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three releases to rename a column, and that is the price of no downtime. It is also the real reason for the pattern: rolling back code does not roll back data, so each step must be independently reversible."}, {"id": "questions_21_deployment_strategies", "label": "Rolling, blue/green and canary", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rolling is the Kubernetes default and what the manifests use, with maxUnavailable: 0 so new pods must become ready before old ones are removed."}, {"id": "questions_21_deployment_migrations_on_startup_limitation", "label": "Migrations on startup do not scale", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two replicas starting simultaneously both try to migrate and a failed migration crash-loops the pod; the fix is a Kubernetes Job or init container that runs migrations once before the deployment rolls."}, {"id": "questions_21_deployment_database_per_service", "label": "Database per service", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A shared server is a cost decision; a shared database is an architecture decision and a bad one. Compose runs one PostgreSQL server with seven separate databases."}], "edges": [{"source": "questions_21_deployment_independent_deployment", "target": "questions_21_deployment_question", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_21_deployment_one_image_all_environments", "target": "questions_21_deployment_question", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_21_deployment_backwards_compatibility", "target": "questions_21_deployment_independent_deployment", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_21_deployment_expand_contract", "target": "questions_21_deployment_backwards_compatibility", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_21_deployment_strategies", "target": "questions_21_deployment_question", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_21_deployment_migrations_on_startup_limitation", "target": "questions_21_deployment_question", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_21_deployment_database_per_service", "target": "questions_06_advantages_and_challenges_independence", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.95, "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_21_deployment_strategies", "target": "questions_22_docker_and_kubernetes_liveness_vs_readiness", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/21-deployment.md", "sou